---
id: org.dxos.plugin.mcp
name: McpPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A plugin that lets users configure MCP (Model Context Protocol) server connections.
Each configured server appears as a toggleable blueprint in conversations,
providing dynamically discovered tools to the AI assistant via the existing
`@dxos/mcp-client` pipeline.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |

## Types

```mdl
type McpServerEntry
  fields:
    id: string                    # unique identifier
    name: string                  # display name
    url: string                   # server endpoint URL
    protocol: sse | http          # transport protocol
```

```mdl
type Settings
  fields:
    servers: McpServerEntry[]     # list of configured MCP servers
```

## Components

```mdl
component McpSettings
  desc: Settings form for managing MCP server connections.
  props:
    settings: Settings
    onSettingsChange: (updater: (current: Settings) => Settings) => void
  state:
    none
  actions:
    addServer()                   # appends a new empty server entry
    removeServer(id: string)      # removes a server entry by id
    updateServer(id: string, field: string, value: string)  # updates a field on a server entry
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
    │ MCP Servers                     │
    ├─────────────────────────────────┤
    │ ┌─────────────────────────────┐ │
    │ │ Server name  [__________]   │ │
    │ │ Server URL   [__________]   │ │
    │ │ Protocol     [HTTP ▼]       │ │
    │ │ [Remove server]             │ │
    │ └─────────────────────────────┘ │
    │ ... (repeat per server)         │
    ├─────────────────────────────────┤
    │ [Add server]                    │
    └─────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Configure MCP Servers

  req F-1.1: User can add a new MCP server entry via the settings UI.
  req F-1.2: User can remove an existing server entry.
  req F-1.3: User can edit the name, URL, and protocol of a server entry.
  req F-1.4: Server entries are persisted to localStorage via KVS atom.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Blueprint Generation

  req F-2.1: Each configured server produces a BlueprintDefinition.
  req F-2.2: Blueprint key is prefixed with org.dxos.blueprint.mcp and suffixed with server id.
  req F-2.3: Blueprint includes mcpServers array with the server URL and protocol.
  req F-2.4: Blueprints are toggleable per-conversation via the existing blueprint system.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Dynamic Tool Discovery

  req F-3.1:
    when: a conversation enables an MCP blueprint
    then: the assistant runtime connects to the MCP server and discovers tools dynamically
    note: handled by existing @dxos/mcp-client and @dxos/assistant infrastructure
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
test T-1: Add server entry
  given: settings UI is open with no servers configured
  when: user clicks "Add server"
  then:
    - a new server entry appears with empty name and URL
    - protocol defaults to HTTP
```

```mdl
test T-2: Remove server entry
  given: settings UI is open with one server configured
  when: user clicks "Remove server"
  then: the server entry is removed from the list
```

```mdl
test T-3: Edit server entry
  given: settings UI is open with one server configured
  when: user changes the name, URL, and protocol fields
  then: the server entry reflects the updated values
```

```mdl
test T-4: Blueprint generated per server
  given: two MCP servers are configured in settings
  when: blueprint definitions are activated
  then:
    - two BlueprintDefinition contributions are produced
    - each has a unique key derived from the server id
    - each blueprint includes the server URL and protocol in mcpServers
```

```mdl
test T-5: Settings persistence
  given: user adds a server with name "My MCP" and URL "https://example.com/mcp"
  when: the page is reloaded
  then: the server entry is still present with the same values
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: dxos.spec/ext/type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: dxos.spec/ext/feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext test
  uri: dxos.spec/ext/test@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```
